{
  "title": "University Payroll: 2,000 Employees",
  "view": "learning.sql-case-studies",
  "questions": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "question": "Tables and calculation",
      "answer": "employees: id, employee_no, name, department_id, bank_account_id, employment_status.\nsalary_structures: id, employee_id, basic_salary, hra, allowances, deductions, effective_from, effective_to.\npayroll_runs: id, payroll_month, total_employees, total_gross, total_deductions, total_net, status, timestamps.\npayroll_items: id, payroll_run_id, employee_id, gross_salary, deductions, net_salary, status, payment_reference, failure_code.\n\nBasic Rs 50,000 + HRA Rs 20,000 + allowance Rs 10,000 - deductions Rs 5,000 = net Rs 75,000."
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "question": "Approve, freeze and process",
      "answer": "DRAFT -> CALCULATED -> APPROVED -> PROCESSING -> COMPLETED. Freeze approved amounts; corrections use an audited adjustment, reversal or new run. Enforce a unique run/employee combination and payment reference.\n\nProcess 2,000 employees in controlled groups, for example 200 at a time, while tracking each payment separately. SAL-2026-09-EMP0001 identifies a business payment; adjustments need their own references. Employee 700 failing does not undo successful payments for other employees.\n\nKeep PROCESSING while any payment is pending or unknown. Once all outcomes are terminal, use COMPLETED for all success or PARTIALLY_COMPLETED for a mixture of success and confirmed failure. Generate salary slips after confirmed payment."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Calculate and freeze September payroll for 2,000 employees, process ten groups of 200, and trace one employee through bank confirmation and a salary slip.",
  "example_label": "Illustrative production scenario \u2014 fictional educational records",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "lesson-01",
      "title": "Business Scenario",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "paragraphs": [
            "The illustrative university employs 2,000 people. Each example employee has basic \u20b950,000, HRA \u20b920,000, allowance \u20b910,000 and deductions \u20b95,000. Gross is \u20b980,000 and net is \u20b975,000. At this uniform illustrative rate, total net payroll is \u20b9150,000,000 = \u20b915 crore.",
            "Payroll calculation and money movement are separate workflows. Freeze the approved salary snapshot so an edit to next month's salary structure cannot change this month's approved bank request.",
            "Ten scheduling groups contain employees 1\u2013200, 201\u2013400, 401\u2013600, 601\u2013800, 801\u20131000, 1001\u20131200, 1201\u20131400, 1401\u20131600, 1601\u20131800 and 1801\u20132000. A scheduling group is not one atomic bank transaction."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "caption": "Illustrative values only",
          "columns": [
            "Reference",
            "Amount per main request",
            "Scope"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "SAL-2026-09-EMP0001",
              "\u20b975,000",
              "External outcome plus local allocation"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
