    {
      "id": "lesson-05",
      "title": "What Happens Inside the Application",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "paragraphs": [
            "The calculation service selects the salary structure valid for September, computes gross and net using decimal arithmetic, and writes 80000.00, 5000.00 and 75000.00 to payroll_items.id=20001. Run totals are sums of the persisted items, not a repeated estimate.",
            "The approval service locks payroll_runs.id=1, verifies CALCULATED, checks maker/checker permissions and totals, then records approved_by/approved_at and durable outbox work. A second approval sees the new status and returns the existing result.",
            "A worker atomically claims a READY request before contacting the bank outside the database transaction. A lease expiry or worker crash after a send creates uncertainty: reconcile the saved reference before another submission. The callback applies a terminal item outcome once; it does not reopen the historical payroll calculation."
          ]
        },
        {
          "shared": "block-80"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lesson-06",
      "title": "Database Transaction",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "flow",
          "caption": "Transaction boundaries",
          "steps": [
            "BEGIN: lock bank request 30001",
            "Claim READY \u2192 SUBMITTED with lease",
            "COMMIT before bank HTTP call",
            "Submit saved business reference",
            "Verify callback / status query",
            "BEGIN: lock request then payroll item",
            "Set confirmed SUCCESS; audit + slip outbox",
            "COMMIT"
          ]
        },
